$DIR/main.p:11:7: cannot copy an element of type main.Conn: it is an owner
    The container method At gives an element out by value. For an owner that
    would be a second owner of what the element owns, and both would release it.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    To look at an element, use a method that returns a pointer to it:
        p := v.Ptr(i)
    To move an element out, use a method that removes it:
        x := v.Pop()
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3306" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:21:10: cannot copy an element of type main.Conn: it is an owner
    The container method Get gives an element out by value. For an owner that
    would be a second owner of what the element owns, and both would release it.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    To look at a value, use a method that returns a pointer to it:
        p := m.Ptr(k)
    To move a value out, use a method that removes it:
        x, ok := m.Remove(k)
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3306" for a longer explanation)
